# API

Base URL after deployment: the Terraform output `api_url`, of the form
`https://<api-id>.execute-api.${{ values.awsRegion or 'us-east-1' }}.amazonaws.com/${{ stage }}`.

The portal shows the same definition under the API entity of this component.

## Endpoints

| Method | Path | Description | Status |
| ------ | ---- | ----------- | ------ |
| GET | `/health` | Health check, always public | Implemented |
{%- if values.enableCRUD %}
| GET | `/items` | List items (at most 100) | Implemented |
| POST | `/items` | Create an item from a JSON object | Implemented |
| GET | `/items/{id}` | Get an item | Implemented |
| PUT | `/items/{id}` | Replace an item | Implemented |
| DELETE | `/items/{id}` | Delete an item | Implemented |
{%- endif %}
{%- for endpoint in values.endpoints or [] %}
| ${{ endpoint.method }} | `${{ endpoint.path }}` | ${{ (endpoint.description or '') | replace('|', '\\|') | replace('\n', ' ') }} | Answers `501` until implemented |
{%- endfor %}

Errors are JSON objects with a `message`.
{%- if values.enableCRUD %}

### Items

An item is any JSON object. The API adds `id` (UUID), `createdAt` and
`updatedAt` (ISO 8601, UTC). `PUT` replaces every other attribute.

```bash
curl -X POST "$API_URL/items" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"name":"first"}'
```
{%- endif %}

## Authentication
{% if authType == 'jwt' %}
Every endpoint except `/health` needs a JSON Web Token in the `Authorization`
header:

```
Authorization: Bearer <token>
```

The Lambda authorizer in `authorizer/` accepts a token when

- it is signed (RS256, RS384, RS512, ES256 or ES384) by a key published in the
  issuer's key set (`<issuer>/.well-known/jwks.json` unless `jwt_jwks_uri` is
  set),
- its `iss` claim is `${{ values.jwtIssuer }}`,
- its `aud` claim contains `${{ values.jwtAudience }}`,
- it has not expired.

API Gateway caches the decision for a token for five minutes. The function
finds the token's `sub` and `scope` in `event.requestContext.authorizer`.
{% elif authType == 'apikey' %}
Every endpoint except `/health` needs an API key in the `x-api-key` header.
One key, `${{ values.apiName }}-default`, is created with the API. Read its value
with:

```bash
aws apigateway get-api-key --include-value --api-key "$(terraform -chdir=infra output -raw api_key_id)"
```

Add `aws_api_gateway_api_key` and `aws_api_gateway_usage_plan_key` resources
in `infra/auth.tf` for further clients.
{% elif authType == 'cognito' %}
Every endpoint except `/health` needs the ID token of a user of the Cognito
user pool `${{ values.apiName }}` in the `Authorization` header. The pool and an
app client are created with the API (outputs `cognito_user_pool_id` and
`cognito_user_pool_client_id`). Users sign in with their e-mail address; only
administrators create users:

```bash
aws cognito-idp admin-create-user --user-pool-id <pool id> --username user@example.com
```
{% else %}
None. Every endpoint is public. To require authentication later, set
`enable_auth` and `auth_type` in `infra/terraform.tfvars.json`.
{% endif %}
## Limits
{% if values.rateLimiting %}
- The stage accepts ${{ values.requestsPerSecond or 100 }} requests per second per method, with bursts
  up to ${{ (values.requestsPerSecond or 100) * 2 }}. Requests above that get `429`.
{%- if authType == 'apikey' %}
- The usage plan applies the same limit to each API key separately.
{%- endif %}
{%- if values.enableWAF %}
- WAF blocks a client address that sends more than ${{ (values.requestsPerSecond or 100) * 300 }} requests
  in five minutes (${{ values.requestsPerSecond or 100 }} per second on average) with `403`.
{%- endif %}
{%- else %}
- Rate limiting is off: only the account-level API Gateway limits apply.
{%- endif %}
- API Gateway waits at most 29 seconds for the function.
- Request bodies are limited to 10 MB by API Gateway and 6 MB by Lambda.
